  "notes": [
    "largest footprint of the three highway x arterial interchanges here; prefer parclo or diamond when land is constrained.",
    "every loop ramp rises/descends 8 m over a 100 m run on each side (lessons.md:716); the loop's own curvature is not modelled here (straight chords only) -- a real build needs intermediate nodes to keep turn angles sane.",
    "weaving between adjacent loop ramps' merge/diverge points is a known cloverleaf problem (see knowledge.md Traffic 'let traffic exit before new traffic enters'); a collector-distributor road (see collector-distributor.json) fixes it if traffic is heavy."
  ]
